---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="What this blog is, who it is for, and how its articles are checked.">
  <h1>About this blog</h1>
  <p>
    This blog is for freelance marketers who work with U.S. residential real estate brokerages and
    want to use AI for SEO, visibility in AI-powered search, and content planning.
  </p>
  <h2>How articles are made</h2>
  <p>
    AI does the heavy lifting on research and drafting. Every article is then reviewed by a person
    before it is published. Claims link to the sources that directly support them, each source is
    labeled by type, and anything that could not be verified is flagged instead of presented as fact.
  </p>
  <h2>What you will not find here</h2>
  <p>
    Guaranteed rankings, promised AI citations, invented test results, or generic advice for home
    buyers and agents. If a claim is only a hypothesis, the article says so.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
